      "name": "Atelerix",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "African hedgehogs — four-toed hedgehogs of sub-Saharan Africa and the Sahara. The African pygmy hedgehog (Atelerix albiventris) has become a popular pet worldwide, particularly in North America and Japan, though ownership is restricted in some US states. African hedgehogs tend to be smaller and more arid-adapted than their European relatives; some can aestivate during dry season in addition to hibernating in cold seasons. The four-toed hedgehog lacks the first toe on its hind feet, distinguishing it from European species.",
