      "id": "GENUS_HEMIECHINUS",
      "name": "Hemiechinus",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "Long-eared hedgehogs — a genus notable for their large, prominent ears that aid thermoregulation in hot desert environments. The ears radiate heat and provide acute hearing for detecting prey underground. These hedgehogs are faster runners than Erinaceus species and rely less on rolling into a ball, preferring to flee or jab at threats. They inhabit arid and semi-arid regions across Central Asia, South Asia, and North Africa.",
