      "id": "GENUS_HYLOMYS",
      "name": "Hylomys",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "Moonrats and gymnures — the most primitive members of the hedgehog family, lacking spines entirely. Moonrats superficially resemble large shrews or small opossums and represent the closest living relatives of true hedgehogs. The greater moonrat (Echinosorex gymnura) is the largest insectivore in Southeast Asia, reaching 40 cm in body length and smelling powerfully of ammonia. Gymnures are forest floor specialists of Southeast Asian rainforest; the lesser gymnure (Hylomys suillus) is one of the most abundant small mammals in the cloud forests of Borneo.",
